packages/core/EventManager.ts:118-119:
118:    const [mainHostDestinationCalendar] = evt.destinationCalendar ?? [];
119:    if (evt.location === MeetLocationType && mainHostDestinationCalendar.integration !== "google_calendar") {
Line 119 lacks `?.` before `.integration`. Callers do supply empty arrays, e.g. packages/features/bookings/lib/handleCancelBooking.ts:255 `: [],` and packages/features/bookings/lib/handleNewBooking.ts:1067 `: null` (both yield `[]` via `?? []`), so destructuring gives `undefined`. Verified with a node snippet: `const [m] = [] ?? []; m.integration` throws "Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'integration')" when the location is `integrations:google:meet`, while non-Meet locations short-circuit.
